{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794543711422,"sessionID":"ses_e2cdd3a02ffe7tBn2LFIz7jxoD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d323f008001AAw3HbVVt9IHSO","sessionID":"ses_e2cdd3a02ffe7tBn2LFIz7jxoD","messageID":"msg_1d323adc7001gxhYycjfJPqp7W","type":"tool","id":"call_3d3ef7e59c9a41cda73ef330","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md, lines 1-67\n1: ---\n2: title: Feature Catalog Creation References\n3: description: \"Route-map for the create-feature-catalog reference overflow: a worked live-catalog example and a deep-dive pitfalls companion, with the primary workflow held in SKILL.md.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"feature catalog references\"\n6:   - \"feature catalog reference map\"\n7:   - \"feature catalog overflow guidance\"\n8:   - \"feature catalog examples and pitfalls\"\n9:   - \"create feature catalog reference index\"\n10: importance_tier: normal\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.0.1.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Create Feature Catalog - References\n16: \n17: Route-map for the `create-feature-catalog` reference set. The primary authoring contract lives in the packet `SKILL.md`; these references carry only the overflow depth that does not belong inline.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: `../SKILL.md` is the single source of truth for the feature-catalog workflow and rules: when to build a catalog, the canonical package shape, the numbered creation workflow, root-catalog and per-feature requirements, the catalog/playbook boundary, and the ALWAYS/NEVER/ESCALATE rules. Read it first. Load a reference below only when you need the extra depth it names; the workflow is not re-stated here.\n24: \n25: **Core Principle**: Keep the workflow and contract in `SKILL.md`; keep worked depth (a real example, extended pitfall fixes) in single-concern references.\n26: \n27: Two scaffolds live in `../assets/` and are the starting point for actual files:\n28: \n29: - `feature-catalog-template.md`: root catalog scaffold, plus its own when-to-create table, category/file design, authoring notes, and publishing checklist.\n30: - `feature-catalog-snippet-template.md`: per-feature file scaffold, plus its frontmatter contract, authoring notes, and per-feature checklist.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. REFERENCE MAP\n35: \n36: Load the file that matches the current task:\n37: \n38: | Concern | Reference | Load When |\n39: | --- | --- | --- |\n40: | **The workflow and rules**: when to create, package shape, the numbered creation workflow, root-catalog and per-feature requirements, playbook boundary, ALWAYS/NEVER/ESCALATE | [../SKILL.md](../SKILL.md) | Authoring or restructuring any catalog: this is the primary contract, read it first |\n41: | **A worked real-world example**: an annotated walkthrough of the shipped `system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/` package: root-catalog anatomy and a real per-feature file, section by section | [examples.md](examples.md) | Modeling a new catalog on a proven layout, or checking what a good root entry and per-feature file actually look like |\n42: | **Deep-dive pitfalls**: the recurring catalog defects with worked before/after fixes, plus the template-versus-reference split | [common-pitfalls.md](common-pitfalls.md) | A catalog drifts toward roadmap, loses source anchors, breaks slugs, or reads as a wall of prose; reviewing a freshly authored catalog |\n43: \n44: ---\n45: \n46: ## 3. RELATED RESOURCES\n47: \n48: ### Packet\n49: \n50: - [../SKILL.md](../SKILL.md) - the primary feature-catalog workflow and rules contract\n51: - [../assets/feature-catalog-template.md](../assets/feature-catalog-template.md) - root catalog scaffold\n52: - [../assets/feature-catalog-snippet-template.md](../assets/feature-catalog-snippet-template.md) - per-feature file scaffold\n53: \n54: ### Shared sk-doc backbone\n55: \n56: - [quick-reference.md](../../shared/references/quick-reference.md) - condensed commands and file locations\n57: - [validation.md](../../shared/references/validation.md) - quality scoring and validation workflows\n58: - [frontmatter-versioning.md](../../sk-create-frontmatter/references/frontmatter-versioning.md) - 4-part version field rules\n59: \n60: ### Companion packets\n61: \n62: - [create-manual-testing-playbook references](../../sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/README.md) - the validation-package side of the catalog/playbook boundary\n63: - [workflows.md](../../sk-create-quality-control/references/workflows.md) - create-quality-control execution modes\n64: \n65: ### Live example\n66: \n67: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/` - the shipped catalog walked through in [examples.md](examples.md)","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md, lines 1-67\n1: ---\n2: title: Feature Catalog Creation References\n3: description: \"Route-map for the create-feature-catalog reference overflow: a worked live-catalog example and a deep-dive pitfalls companion, with the primary workflow held in SKILL.md.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"feature catalog references\"\n6:   - \"feature catalog reference map\"\n7:   - \"feature catalog overflow guidance\"\n8:   - \"feature catalog examples and pitfalls\"\n9:   - \"create feature catalog reference index\"\n10: importance_tier: normal\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.0.1.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Create Feature Catalog - References\n16: \n17: Route-map for the `create-feature-catalog` reference set. The primary authoring contract lives in the packet `SKILL.md`; these references carry only the overflow depth that does not belong inline.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: `../SKILL.md` is the single source of truth for the feature-catalog workflow and rules: when to build a catalog, the canonical package shape, the numbered creation workflow, root-catalog and per-feature requirements, the catalog/playbook boundary, and the ALWAYS/NEVER/ESCALATE rules. Read it first. Load a reference below only when you need the extra depth it names; the workflow is not re-stated here.\n24: \n25: **Core Principle**: Keep the workflow and contract in `SKILL.md`; keep worked depth (a real example, extended pitfall fixes) in single-concern references.\n26: \n27: Two scaffolds live in `../assets/` and are the starting point for actual files:\n28: \n29: - `feature-catalog-template.md`: root catalog scaffold, plus its own when-to-create table, category/file design, authoring notes, and publishing checklist.\n30: - `feature-catalog-snippet-template.md`: per-feature file scaffold, plus its frontmatter contract, authoring notes, and per-feature checklist.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. REFERENCE MAP\n35: \n36: Load the file that matches the current task:\n37: \n38: | Concern | Reference | Load When |\n39: | --- | --- | --- |\n40: | **The workflow and rules**: when to create, package shape, the numbered creation workflow, root-catalog and per-feature requirements, playbook boundary, ALWAYS/NEVER/ESCALATE | [../SKILL.md](../SKILL.md) | Authoring or restructuring any catalog: this is the primary contract, read it first |\n41: | **A worked real-world example**: an annotated walkthrough of the shipped `system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/` package: root-catalog anatomy and a real per-feature file, section by section | [examples.md](examples.md) | Modeling a new catalog on a proven layout, or checking what a good root entry and per-feature file actually look like |\n42: | **Deep-dive pitfalls**: the recurring catalog defects with worked