{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794543711448,"sessionID":"ses_e2cdd3a02ffe7tBn2LFIz7jxoD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d323f1d7001g1eVE8FC71307d","sessionID":"ses_e2cdd3a02ffe7tBn2LFIz7jxoD","messageID":"msg_1d323adc7001gxhYycjfJPqp7W","type":"tool","id":"call_114c35bc740248ea8ffa887d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"repair path|is offered the command that names the right one|stopped converging\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"31:A doctor bridge passes on its own wording, an explicit-author match on one of its manifest phrases or its runnable string. With the local embedder running it can also pass on meaning, as [command-meaning-matching.md](./command-meaning-matching.md) describes. When none passes and none was typed, the scorer asks `/doctor:helper`'s ranker whether the prompt describes a doctor problem, and if it does the `/doctor:helper` bridge passes so the operator is offered the command that names the right one. Beside a passing skill this needs a wrong state or health check in the prompt, so ordinary requests that share doctor words get no doctor line. A `/doctor:` command counts as typed when the prompt starts with `/doctor:` or when it directly follows `run`, `execute`, `start`, `launch`, `use` or `kick off` outside quotes and backticks. A quoted command or a bare mid-sentence mention does not count. A typed command puts its own passing bridge first. For other prompts, a passing skill stays first and passing doctor bridges sit right after the second passing skill or the only passing skill. This keeps a doctor line within the CLI's three shown results. Doctor bridges never change skill scores. The scorer computes skill ambiguity and abstention as if no doctor bridge existed. The Python native wrapper keeps the same order. A read-only question, such as a list or show prompt, holds every candidate under the read-only confidence floor, unless the prompt names the skill, a command bridge marked `readOnly` matches one of its own phrases, or a skill-specific rule lifts it. A prompt with a no-write phrase, such as `no edits` or `just list`, gets none of these lifts. Mutating bridges stay gated.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31:A doctor bridge passes on its own wording, an explicit-author match on one of its manifest phrases or its runnable string. With the local embedder running it can also pass on meaning, as [command-meaning-matching.md](./command-meaning-matching.md) describes. When none passes and none was typed, the scorer asks `/doctor:helper`'s ranker whether the prompt describes a doctor problem, and if it does the `/doctor:helper` bridge passes so the operator is offered the command that names the right one. Beside a passing skill this needs a wrong state or health check in the prompt, so ordinary requests that share doctor words get no doctor line. A `/doctor:` command counts as typed when the prompt starts with `/doctor:` or when it directly follows `run`, `execute`, `start`, `launch`, `use` or `kick off` outside quotes and backticks. A quoted command or a bare mid-sentence mention does not count. A typed command puts its own passing bridge first. For other prompts, a passing skill stays first and passing doctor bridges sit right after the second passing skill or the only passing skill. This keeps a doctor line within the CLI's three shown results. Doctor bridges never change skill scores. The scorer computes skill ambiguity and abstention as if no doctor bridge existed. The Python native wrapper keeps the same order. A read-only question, such as a list or show prompt, holds every candidate under the read-only confidence floor, unless the prompt names the skill, a command bridge marked `readOnly` matches one of its own phrases, or a skill-specific rule lifts it. A prompt with a no-write phrase, such as `no edits` or `just list`, gets none of these lifts. Mutating bridges stay gated.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"repair path|is offered the command that names the right one|stopped converging\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794543710679,"end":1794543711448}}}}
